<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 389 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Conon of Athens</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conon was an Athenian admiral of the late 5th and early 4th centuries BCE. He escaped the Athenian defeat at Aegospotami in 405 BCE and took refuge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, and later commanded a fleet for the Persian king. In 394 BCE he and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> Pharnabazus destroyed the Spartan fleet off Knidos, ending Spartan naval supremacy, and he then helped rebuild the Long Walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conon.jpg" alt="Conon" width="320" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Published by Guillaume Rouille (1518?-1589) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
